cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CausalRLBreaker in your research, please cite this work."
title: "CausalRLBreaker: Causally Guided Reinforcement Learning for LLM Security Testing"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Zeinaliashtiyani
    given-names: Parisa

version: 1.0.0

repository-code: "https://github.com/parisazeynaly/Security-Testing-of-Large-Language-Models-via-Reinforcement-Learning"

license: Apache-2.0

abstract: "CausalRLBreaker is a research framework for automated black-box security testing of large language models. It combines PPO-based adaptive prompt search with an interpretable six-factor representation, FCI/PAG structural discovery, SCM-informed intermediate feedback, and causal-graph-guided action selection."

keywords:
  - large language models
  - LLM security
  - AI security
  - red teaming
  - causal machine learning
  - causal reinforcement learning
  - reinforcement learning
  - structural causal models
  - causal discovery
  - PPO
